            <ArticleTitle>Linear densities in mitochondria of human myocardial cells.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>790-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ultrastructural study of myocardial biopsies from 5 patients who underwent myocardial revascularization procedures because of impending infarction showed mitochondria with linear densities. These densities, which occupied the intracristal space, appeared to have a high protein but low mineral content. It is suggested that linear densities may be an expression of severe, acute myocardial cell injury.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
